    "reply": "EGFR is extensively catalogued in ClinVar with a large number of distinct missense and other variants along the coding sequence, reflecting the diversity of alterations reported for this gene, while a set of clinical trials addresses EGFR-mutant non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) treatment and monitoring.\n\n## ClinVar Variant Landscape\n\nClinVar records document numerous EGFR sequence variants referenced to transcript NM_005228.5, including substitutions such as c.840C>A (p.Asn280Lys) [6], c.664C>T (p.Arg222Cys) [7], c.494G>A (p.Arg165Gln) [8], c.652C>A (p.Gln218Lys) [9], c.1813A>G (p.Thr605Ala) [10], c.2653T>G (p.Ser885Ala) [11], c.991G>A (p.Gly331Arg) [12], c.1822T>A (p.Trp608Arg) [13], c.1559C>T (p.Pro520Leu) [14], c.2741C>G (p.Pro914Arg) [15], c.2619A>T (p.Gly873=) [16], c.2339T>C (p.Ile780Thr) [17], c.1670A>G (p.Gln557Arg) [18], c.721A>G (p.Thr241Ala) [19], c.3031G>C (p.Val1011Leu) [20], c.3209G>A (p.Ser1070Asn) [21], c.1463C>G (p.Thr488Ser) [22], c.2917C>G (p.Arg973Gly) [23], c.1049C>G (p.Ser350Cys) [24], c.1675C>T (p.His559Tyr) [25], c.1975G>C (p.Val659Leu) [26], c.2833A>G (p.Met945Val) [27], c.541C>G (p.Gln181Glu) [28], c.1739T>C (p.Ile580Thr) [29], and c.1582A>G (p.Asn528Asp) [30].\n\n## Treatment-Focused Trials\n\nSeveral trials address EGFR-TKI therapy in NSCLC directly. One trial is named A Retrospective Study of EGFR-TKIs,Gefitinib, Erlotinib and Osimertinib in NSCLC Patients Treatment [1]. Another is named Survival Outcome of EGFR-TKI in Uncommon EGFR Mutant Advanced NSCLC [2]. A further trial is named Osimertinib for Advanced EGFR-positive NSCLC Patients [3].\n\n## Complications and Cellular Therapy\n\nBeyond frontline TKI use, one trial is named CSF Analysis in EGFR Mutant Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer With Leptomeningeal Disease [4], addressing central nervous system spread. An investigational cellular approach is captured in a trial named EGFR/B7H3 CAR-T on Lung Cancer and Triple Negative Breast Cancer [5].",
